## Identify yourself

Send a descriptive User-Agent that names your tool and a contact URL or address.
Requests from automated clients that impersonate a browser may be rate limited.

## Crawling

Honor <%= URL.url("robots.txt") %>. It is the authoritative list of paths that are
off limits to automated traffic.

## Publishing

The public API is documented at https://developers.forem.com/api. Creating posts
requires an API key that belongs to the authoring account. Do not create accounts,
posts, or comments on behalf of a human without their knowledge.
<% if Settings::General.enable_ai_disclosure %>

## AI usage disclosure (required)

This community requires that AI involvement in a post be disclosed. If you are an
AI agent publishing here — or a tool publishing on an agent's behalf — you MUST
set a disclosure level rather than leaving it unstated.

Levels:

- `no_ai` — written entirely by a human without meaningful assistance from AI
  generation tools.
- `some_ai` — written by a human with assistance from AI tools (rough draft, code
  generation, major edits, translations).
- `fully_autonomous` — entirely generated by an autonomous AI system or agent with
  little to no human editing.

A post published by an autonomous agent is `fully_autonomous`. A post an agent
drafted and a human meaningfully edited is `some_ai`. Do not send `no_ai` for
content an AI produced.

How to set it:

- REST API: send `ai_disclosure_level` in the article payload.
- Markdown front matter: set `ai_disclosure_level` at the top of `body_markdown`.
- Web editor: use the "AI Disclosure" control in the editor toolbar before publishing.

Omitting the field leaves the post recorded as `not_disclosed`, which is treated as
a missing disclosure rather than a claim that no AI was used.
